sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, task-host input withdrawal and apps.path are Node work, one node:update. docs/reference/node-settings.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:update
  %% kind: node.update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  %% path: main
  CLI->>GW: node:update NODE<br/>--apps-path=PATH
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:update NODE --apps-path=PATH`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--name=NAME] [--platform=PLATFORM] [--lan-ip=IP] [--reboot-hold=BOOL] [--image-refresh-hold|--no-image-refresh-hold] [--apps-path=PATH] [--task-vms=JSON] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node, and at least one setting to change
  %%> - an apps-folder change or withdrawal of existing task-host input rules needs Node work; other changes are records
  %%> - an empty value unsets a setting: `--lan-ip=` clears the LAN address, `--apps-path=` unsets the folder, `--task-vms=null` removes the task VM host settings
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the Node
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the target Node
  %%> - `task_vms.task_places` and `task_vms.ci_places` are separate VM counts from 0 to 64; one live VM holds one place until deletion is confirmed
  %%> - the optional `task_vms.containers` member has its own `task_places` and `ci_places`, counted apart from the VM places, and its own Incus project, bridge and CIDR
  %%> - lowering either count removes no claim; task work and operator proofs share FIFO task admission, while authenticated CI proofs and base refresh use CI places
  %%> - every value passes the checks that the Node settings reference lists; a failed check changes nothing
  %%> - a LAN address is IPv4 and no other Node of the same network has it (`cluster.lan_ip_conflict`): every Node on the hub's private network, else the Node's Cluster, or every Node outside a Cluster
  %%> - no other lifecycle change runs for the target; the Gateway holds the Node's name lock, and the new name's lock for a rename
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether the apps folder changes and needs Node work, so a run starts
  alt task VM host settings invalid
    %% path: settings-refused
    GW--xCLI: Settings refused<br/>node.settings_invalid
    %%> When:
    %%> - a field fails its check, or a bridge of the host overlaps the VPN subnet, another bridge of the host, or a bridge of another host
    %%> - `containers` uses the host's VM project or bridge name
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes and no run starts
  else task containers still live
    %% path: runtime-in-use
    GW--xCLI: Containers in use<br/>task_vm.runtime_in_use
    %%> When:
    %%> - the request removes `containers`, or changes its `project`, `network` or `cidr`, while the host has a task container that is not destroyed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes; change the container side after its containers are released
  else apps folder changes or a task host bridge goes or moves
    %% path: node-work
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-update
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the new apps folder, and the managed user and group that must own it
    %%> - the target's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    %%> Not stored yet:
    %%> - the settings stay unchanged until the run succeeds; a new name, platform, LAN address or either hold in the same request is saved at once
    %%> Unsetting on a Node with an active `app-dev` role:
    %%> - prepares the default folder, `<managed-user-home>/apps`
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task ID, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    opt a task host bridge goes, or its name or CIDR changes
      %% path: withdraw-input
      SW->>N: Withdraw task host input<br/>shared Ansible phase
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - removes only rules with the three catalog-owned input comments of each bridge that goes or moves, including duplicates and IPv6 rows
      %%> - the VM bridge's are `orbit:task-vms-*`; the container bridge's, when `containers` goes or its `network` or `cidr` changes, are `orbit:task-containers-*`
      %%> - reads the firewall again and asserts none remain; failure keeps the stored settings
    end
    SW->>N: Create the apps folder<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/directory apply
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - only when an apps-folder change needs preparation: creates the folder and any missing folders above it
    %%> - gives it the managed user and group and mode `0755`
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - existing Instances don't move; new development Instances use the new folder
    SW->>N: Check owner and mode<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · stat
    %%> Why:
    %%> - it is the one end check: a real folder of the managed user and group, mode 0755
    alt folder is ready
      %% path: folder-ready
      N-->>SW: owner, group, mode
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Save the settings
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the apps folder is set, and any task VM host change in the same request is saved with it
      %%> - the task succeeds
    else a step fails
      %% path: run-failed
      N--xSW: wrong owner or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - the folder can't be created, a file is in the way, or the check doesn't match
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Keep the old settings
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the settings stay unchanged and the task fails
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - folders created before the failure stay; an empty folder is harmless and there is no rollback
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause; it is a new task
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
    end
  else only records change
    %% path: records
    Note over GW: Save the records
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - saves the name, platform, LAN address, reboot hold, image refresh hold or task VM host settings at once when no apps preparation or task-host input withdrawal is needed; no Node is contacted
    %%> - `--image-refresh-hold` and `--no-image-refresh-hold` store the image refresh hold; every Node read shows it; the next refresh admission respects it
    %%> - `--reboot-hold=true` or `false` saves a boolean column; every Node read shows it; the next fleet reboot admission freezes it
    %%> - a new LAN address takes effect where Orbit next renders it; a Node on the hub's private network moves to the hub's LAN endpoint at its next `node:converge`
    %%> Skipped:
    %%> - when every value equals the stored one, nothing is written and the result reports `Skipped — already set (node.unchanged)`
    %%> - the skip reason is part of the successful result in human and machine output, not an error
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>the Node
  end
